> >   O - a newt corpse.
> >   :
> >   There is an altar to Ptah (lawful) here.
> > 
> > Hey, hey, hey! Let's convert this sucker!
> > 
> >   #offer
> >   What do you want to sacrifice? [rO or ?*]? O
> >   You have a strong feeling that Thoth is angry...
> >   Your sacrifice is consumed in a burst of flame!
> >   Ptah accepts your allegience.
> >   You have a sudden sense of a new direction.
> > 
> > I got my alignment converted, for a stinking _newt_
> > corpse????
> 
> From the above spoiler: "If your god is angry with you when you try to
> convert an altar, _you_ will be converted to the altar's god instead."

This is incorrect.  You will convert yourself if you try to convert an
altar when your alignment is negative.  Whether or not your god is
angry with you does not matter.  The distinction is important because
negative alignment goes away as you kill hostile monsters, but angry
gods need to be appeased by sacrificing.
